.\" Manual page for the FxSound Linux port.
.\"
.\" Kept in packaging/ rather than packaging/debian/ because every package installs it: the
.\" systemd unit says Documentation=man:fxsound(1), and a unit that names a manual page nobody
.\" ships is worse than no line at all. The option list is taken from
.\" crates/fxsound-app/src/cli.rs; if an option is added there and not here, the two have
.\" drifted and cli.rs is the one that is right. The D-Bus section follows
.\" crates/fxsound-app/src/dbus.rs the same way. packaging/check-manpage.sh compares the page
.\" with both files — ci.yml runs it on every push, release.yml before a tag is built — so the
.\" drift is refused rather than hoped against.
.\"
